### Live Log realtime server — manual requests
#
# Open this file with the REST Client extension (VS Code) or the HTTP Client
# (JetBrains IDEs) and press "Send Request" on any block below. Start the server
# first:
#
#   cd server
#   npm install
#   cp tokens.example.json tokens.json
#   LIVELOG_TOKENS_FILE=./tokens.json npm run dev
#
# The token used here is the placeholder from tokens.example.json — it only
# works once you have copied that file to tokens.json. Change @token below to
# match whatever you put there.
#
# Open the viewer on the same channel first to see these arrive:
#   http://localhost:4503 (VITE_LIVELOG_URL=http://localhost:4504)

@base = http://localhost:4504
@token = tk_live_replace_me_default
@channel = default


### Health — is the process up, and how many viewers are attached?
# 200 { "ok": true, "uptime": 42, "channels": 1, "subscribers": 1 }
GET {{base}}/healthz


### Channels with recent traffic — the same list the viewer's sidebar shows
# 200 { "channels": [{ "name": "default", "subscribers": 1, "recent": 3, "lastAt": 1791330135123 }] }
GET {{base}}/api/channels


### Send: debug
# 202 { "ok": true, "seq": 1, "timestamp": 1791330135123 }
POST {{base}}/api/log
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "channel": "{{channel}}",
  "level": "debug",
  "source": "ManualTest",
  "message": "Loading configuration",
  "data": { "version": "1.0.0" }
}


### Send: info
POST {{base}}/api/log
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "channel": "{{channel}}",
  "level": "info",
  "source": "GameClient",
  "message": "Player connected",
  "data": { "playerId": 123, "roomId": "room_01" }
}


### Send: warn
POST {{base}}/api/log
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "channel": "{{channel}}",
  "level": "warn",
  "source": "GameClient",
  "message": "Missing configuration",
  "data": { "key": "gameConfig" }
}


### Send: error
POST {{base}}/api/log
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "channel": "{{channel}}",
  "level": "error",
  "source": "GameClient",
  "message": "Connection failed",
  "data": { "error": "Network timeout", "attempt": 3 }
}


### Send without `source` and `data` — both are optional
POST {{base}}/api/log
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "channel": "{{channel}}",
  "level": "info",
  "message": "Bare minimum log"
}


### Send with a non-object `data` — any JSON value is accepted
POST {{base}}/api/log
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "channel": "{{channel}}",
  "level": "info",
  "message": "String payload",
  "data": "just a string"
}


### ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
### Failure cases — these are expected to fail, and show what the viewer's
### sender will get back. Each block names the status it should return.
### ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

### 401 — no Authorization header
POST {{base}}/api/log
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "channel": "{{channel}}",
  "level": "info",
  "message": "Missing token"
}


### 401 — unknown token
POST {{base}}/api/log
Authorization: Bearer tk_live_wrong
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "channel": "{{channel}}",
  "level": "info",
  "message": "Bad token"
}


### 403 — valid token, channel it does not own
# The example token list grants "default" and the other token "other-project",
# so a single token writing elsewhere is forbidden rather than unauthorized.
POST {{base}}/api/log
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "channel": "other-project",
  "level": "info",
  "message": "Wrong channel"
}


### 400 — unknown level
POST {{base}}/api/log
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "channel": "{{channel}}",
  "level": "trace",
  "message": "Bad level"
}


### 400 — invalid channel name (only [a-zA-Z0-9._-], 1-64 chars)
POST {{base}}/api/log
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "channel": "has spaces",
  "level": "info",
  "message": "Bad channel"
}


### 400 — empty message
POST {{base}}/api/log
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "channel": "{{channel}}",
  "level": "info",
  "message": ""
}


### 400 — body is not valid JSON
POST {{base}}/api/log
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

not json at all


### 405 — GET on the ingest path (it only accepts POST)
GET {{base}}/api/log


### 404 — unknown path
GET {{base}}/api/nope
